{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/443351-what-s-your-vampire-fanmix","id":443351,"title":"What's your Vampire fanmix?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-15T17:19:11-07:00","id":443351,"title":"What's your Vampire fanmix?","content":"I make two kinds of playlists- soundtracks for campaigns and fanmixes, collections of songs that capture the mood the the setting. So has anyone made a VtR fanmix? Here's mine-<br /> <br /> Vampire-<br /> Frigid Spring- Chairlift<br /> Mowgli's Road- Marina and the Diamonds<br /> Black Dresses- The Builders and the Butchers<br /> Pumpkin Tide- Michael Guy Bowman<br /> Purple Haze- Jimi Hendrix<br /> In the Court of the Crimson King- King Crimson<br /> From the Ritz to the Rubble- Arctic Monkeys<br /> Ballroom Blitz- Sweet<br /> The Rose with the Broken Neck- Jack White<br /> Hurricane- MS MR<br /> Bloody Stream- Coda<br /> Dance Floor- The Apples in Stereo<br /> Let's Kill Tonight- Panic! at the Disco<br /> Days Go On- Greg Laswell<br /> Mosquito- Yeah Yeah Yeahs<br /> Satin in a Coffin- Modest Mouse<br /> Bad Blood- Bastille<br /> Road to Nowhere- Talking Heads<br /> Tigerlily- La Roux<br /> This Town Ain't Big Enough- Sparks<br /> Helena Beat- Foster the People<br /> All Hail Dracula- Someone Still Loves You<br /> The Dark of the Matinee- Franz Ferdinand","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T20:03:02-07:00","id":446969,"title":"","content":"I do the same -- my soundtracks tend to be instrumental and in the background, but what I play while I'm setting up is very different. They're usually things the players recognize and relate to -- often from movies more than for any other reason, so the connection is very obvious.<br /> Some of the songs that get in this rotation include:<br /> Tamara Rhodes-- Live Forever (Theme to the series Blood Ties)<br /> Sting -- Moon Over Bourbon Street<br /> Jace Everett -- Bad Things<br /> Ego Likeness-- Treacherous Thing<br /> Siouxie &amp; the Banshees -- Face to Face<br /> Jen Titus -- Oh Death<br /> Concrete Blonde -- Bloodletting, Sky is a Poisonous Garden, Darkening of the Light, the Beast (I may slip Tomorrow, Wendy on to scare the players)<br /> Florence and the Machine -- Cosmic Love (Mekhet figure heavily in my setting, so the references to darkness seem to work)<br /> <br /> Again, not necessarily songs that are lyrically in tune with the setting, just what I play to get folks into the general ballpark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T10:13:05-07:00","id":450566,"title":"","content":"My personal mix for Requiem<br /> <br /> <b>Meat Loaf</b>-Bat Out of Hell<br /> <b>Creedence Clearwater Revival</b>-Bad Moon Rising<br /> <b>KISS</b>-Strutter<br /> <b>Saxon</b>-Wheels of Steel<br /> <b>The Allman Brothers</b>-Ramblin' Man<br /> <b>The Doobie Brothers</b>-China Grove<br /> <b>Steve Earle</b>-Copperhead Road<br /> <b>Iron Maiden</b>-Wasted Years<br /> <b>Judas Priest</b>-Living After Midnight<br /> <b>Nazareth</b>-Hair of the Dog<br /> <b>AC/DC-</b>Highway to Hell<br /> <b>Alice Cooper</b>-Go To Hell<br 